--- body ---
## Context

The UX audit (0152, PR #174) found two adjacent contributor-onboarding
gaps, both verified by the developer persona:

- **F16**: no `CONTRIBUTING.md` exists anywhere. `AGENTS.md` documents
  autonomous *agent* policy (pick/safety/merge gates), not the *human*
  contributor workflow — branch naming, how to submit a patch, code
  style, test policy.
- **F17**: adding a subcommand requires reconstructing a checklist from
  four separate files. Verified: the dispatch switch lives in
  `src/go/main.go` (~lines 190–222), the command registry in
  `src/go/helptext.go` (the `commands` slice), plus a new command file,
  a `tests/test_<cmd>.sh`, and a `TEST_SUITES` entry in the `Makefile`.
  `TestDispatchRegistrySync` (`src/go/erg_test.go:407`) is a good safety
  net that catches drift, but the *workflow* is nowhere documented.

These are one document: the subcommand checklist is a section *inside* a
contributor guide. Filing them together avoids a premature split.

## Relevant files

- (new) `CONTRIBUTING.md` — the contributor guide
- `src/go/helptext.go` — `commands` slice (registry)
- `src/go/main.go` — dispatch switch (~190–222)
- `src/go/erg_test.go:407` — `TestDispatchRegistrySync` (the safety net to cite)
- `Makefile` — `TEST_SUITES` (the test-registration step)
- `tests/README.md` — existing test policy to cross-link, not duplicate
- `README.md`, `AGENTS.md` — link to CONTRIBUTING from a discoverable spot

## Actions

1. Write `CONTRIBUTING.md` covering: build/test loop (`make build`,
   `make test`, single-suite `make test-<cmd>`), branch naming, the
   merge-request workflow, where the test policy lives (link
   `tests/README.md`), and the Go version (link `go.mod`).
2. Add an explicit "Adding a subcommand" checklist: (a) create
   `src/go/<cmd>.go` with `summary<Cmd>` / `help<Cmd>` / `cmd<Cmd>`,
   (b) register in the `commands` slice in `helptext.go`, (c) add a
   dispatch case in `main.go`, (d) create `tests/test_<cmd>.sh`,
   (e) add `<cmd>` to `TEST_SUITES` in the Makefile — and note that
   `TestDispatchRegistrySync` + `_test-lint` enforce steps (b)/(c)/(e).
3. Link CONTRIBUTING.md from README and/or AGENTS.md so a human finds it.

## Test

Source-inspection guard (no subprocess) in `tests/test_docs.sh`:

```sh
# CONTRIBUTING.md exists and lists every file the subcommand checklist touches
for token in helptext.go main.go TEST_SUITES test_; do
    grep -q "$token" CONTRIBUTING.md || fail "CONTRIBUTING.md omits $token"
done
```

Catches a wrong implementation (a stub CONTRIBUTING.md missing the
checklist), not merely a differently-worded one — the negative control
is the current absent file.

## Verification

- [ ] `CONTRIBUTING.md` exists and is linked from a discoverable place
- [ ] The add-a-subcommand checklist names all five touch-points and the
      enforcing tests
- [ ] A new contributor can follow it end-to-end without reading source
- [ ] Guard test fails pre-fix (no file), passes post-fix

## Invariants

- Do not duplicate `tests/README.md` — link it.
- Keep `AGENTS.md` agent-policy-only; CONTRIBUTING.md is the human doc.
- `make test` stays green.

## Exit criteria

- A human contributor guide exists with a complete, accurate
  add-a-subcommand checklist, discoverable from README/AGENTS, guarded
  by a doc test.
